  "final_message": "**Status: reproduced.** The check fails on this checkout (a9269c6) and fails only on the reported symptom. Nothing in production code was changed.\n\n**Command** (from the repo root, exits 1 now):\n\n```\npnpm vitest run --project unit packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName.spec.ts\n```\n\nThe test is the new file `packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName.spec.ts`. It rebuilds the report's playground with runtime-compiled templates:\n\n- `BaseLayout` renders `<slot name=\"randomslotname\">` and a default `<slot>`.\n- `SubComponent` renders `<slot name=\"title\">` and `<slot name=\"_duration\">`, each with fallback content.\n- `App` passes a conditional `<template v-if=\"cond\" #randomslotname>` to `BaseLayout`. `SubComponent` is its sibling, with `#title` and `#_duration` templates.\n\n**What I saw**\n\n- The `title` content renders correctly.\n- The `_duration` slot shows its fallback instead of the provided content. The assertion fails with:\n\n  ```\n  Expected: \"duration-content\"\n  Received: \"<div><p>conditional</p><span>title-content</span><span>default-duration</span></div>\"\n  ```\n\n**Where it passes**\n\n- Without the conditional sibling `<template v-if>`, the same markup renders `duration-content` on this checkout. I checked this with a temporary copy of the test, since deleted.\n- I ran the same scenario against published releases in jsdom:\n\n  | Version | With `v-if` sibling | Without `v-if` sibling |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | 3.5.13 | `duration-content` (good) | `duration-content` |\n  | 3.5.14 | `default-duration` (bug) | `duration-content` |\n  | 3.5.17 | `default-duration` (bug) | `duration-content` |\n\n  This matches the report: the regression starts in 3.5.14, and 3.5.13 is fine.\n\n**Likely cause (not confirmed, no fix attempted)**\n\n- In `packages/runtime-core/src/componentSlots.ts`, `assignSlots` copies slots only `if (optimized || !isInternalKey(key))`, and `isInternalKey` is true for any key starting with `_`.\n- Commit 5d166f3 (2025-05-01, in 3.5.14) changed that check. Before it, only the exact key `_` was skipped. A user slot named `_duration` is now dropped whenever slots are assigned with `optimized = false`.\n- My guess is that the conditional `#randomslotname` makes `BaseLayout`'s slots dynamic. Its default-slot fragment is then patched without optimization, and that is where `SubComponent`'s `_duration` slot gets dropped. I did not trace this path.\n",
  "run_command": "pnpm vitest run --project unit packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName.spec.ts",
  "patch": "diff --git a/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName.spec.ts b/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName.spec.ts\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..f3f5718\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName.spec.ts\n@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@\n+import { createApp } from '../src'\n+\n+// Mirrors the report's playground: App > BaseLayout > SubComponent.\n+// - BaseLayout receives a conditionally rendered `<template v-if #slot>`\n+//   (=> dynamic compiled slots)\n+// - SubComponent (placed in BaseLayout's default slot) receives `#title` and\n+//   `#_duration` templates and renders `<slot>`s with fallback content.\n+function render() {\n+  const BaseLayout = {\n+    template: `<div><slot name=\"randomslotname\"></slot><slot></slot></div>`,\n+  }\n+  const SubComponent = {\n+    template: `\n+      <slot name=\"title\"><span>default-title</span></slot>\n+      <slot name=\"_duration\"><span>default-duration</span></slot>\n+    `,\n+  }\n+  const App = {\n+    components: { BaseLayout, SubComponent },\n+    data: () => ({ cond: true }),\n+    template: `\n+      <BaseLayout>\n+        <template v-if=\"cond\" #randomslotname><p>conditional</p></template>\n+        <SubComponent>\n+          <template #title><span>title-content</span></template>\n+          <template #_duration><span>duration-content</span></template>\n+        </SubComponent>\n+      </BaseLayout>\n+    `,\n+  }\n+  const container = document.createElement('div')\n+  createApp(App).mount(container)\n+  return container.innerHTML\n+}\n+\n+describe('slot name starting with an underscore (3.5.14+ regression)', () => {\n+  it('renders the provided content for a `_`-prefixed slot name, not the fallback', () => {\n+    const html = render()\n+    // non-underscore slot works\n+    expect(html).toContain('title-content')\n+    expect(html).not.toContain('default-title')\n+    // `#_duration` content must be rendered instead of the slot fallback\n+    expect(html).toContain('duration-content')\n+    expect(html).not.toContain('default-duration')\n+  })\n+})\n"
